<h2 id="w1">3. W1: T5 misses the software join poll</h2>
<div class="quote"><div class="who">Wade, on <code>h/tron/models/self_attention.hpp:1131</code></div>
<p>T5 is only timed here, inside <code>stream_hw_joins</code> (the HW join). In SW-only layers the join waits for peer partials in the poll at <code>run_joins</code>: <code>if (!join_hw &amp;&amp; plan_state.sections_left[kv_head]) continue;  // poll</code>. That spin is never timed. So on a CPU-attention run <code>join_wait_cycles</code> reads 0 even when workers are spinning on load imbalance; the <code>"join_wait_cycles":0</code> in the PR description's sample comes from exactly that config. The Note and README say T5 ends when "an FPGA pass or the other workers' software partials become ready", which suggests SW waits are included.</p>
