<p>In serving (rinzler, with continuous batching), one scheduler serves every request of a model [src/rinzler.cpp:2130, :3236]. Each forward walks the whole token tree (every live request's tokens, shared prefixes merged) [full.hpp:1968 onward]. An edge is a run of tokens between two branch points of that tree. A KV entry is the stored key and value of one token in the attention cache. On every edge of a request still in the tree, the walk turns the tokens that have no KV entry yet into token jobs, up to a per-forward token limit (a soft limit <code>live_token_limit</code> and a hard limit <code>capacity_limit</code> [full.hpp:1896-1897, :2111-2129, :2472]). Tokens beyond the limit wait for the next forward [full.hpp:2488]. A prompt enters in chunks of 128 tokens by default (the environment variable <code>TRON_PER_USER_PROMPT_CHUNK_LIMIT</code> changes the chunk size) [src/tron/generation/context.cpp:40-42, h/libtron.hpp:196-204]. Every chunk registers a listener on its node [src/tron/scheduler/full.cpp:191-193]. The walk gives that listener to the chunk's last token [full.hpp:2465-2478]. Nothing keeps a prompt chunk in a forward of its own. So a forward with one user in prefill (prefill = feeding the user's prompt tokens into the KV cache, 128 per chunk by default) and seven in decode holds 128 prompt jobs (one with a listener) plus 7 decode jobs (each with a listener). Its class is <code>prompt_or_mixed</code>, and the 7 decode jobs' visits land there.</p>
